  m_Name: Equilibruim
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonId: What is Equilibrium
  lessonTitle: What is Equilibrium
  lessonImage: {fileID: 0}
  popupDescription: "<b><#E09500>Equilibrium</color></b> means the forces and moments
    acting on a structure are balanced. Downward bridge loads are balanced by
    reactions from the supports. The members and connections must also be strong
    enough to carry those loads.\n\nThis lesson has been added to your
    <b><#E09500>Almanac</color></b>."
  almanacImage: {fileID: 0}
  lessonDescription: "Structural <b><#E09500>Equilibrium</color></b> is the condition
    in which the <b><#E09500>forces and moments acting on a structure are
    balanced</color></b>. Both force balance and moment balance are needed for a
    stationary bridge.\n\nThe weight of the bridge and a crossing vehicle act
    downward. The supports provide <b><#E09500>upward reactions</color></b> that
    help balance these loads. As a vehicle changes position, the forces carried
    by the members and supports change too. If forces or moments are unbalanced,
    the structure may move or rotate.\n\nEquilibrium alone does
    <b><#E09500>not mean a bridge is safe for any load</color></b>. Its members,
    connections, and supports must also have enough strength and stability to
    carry the required loads without failing."
